      "lede": "On August 12, Judge Bostwick entered an Order on Motion to Compel (Dkt. 366), resolving the compel motion Trustee Donald Lassman filed August 10 (Dkt. 359) — the same motion for which the court set a hearing on August 10 (Dkt. 360). The order arrived the same day an objection was filed at Dkt. 365, indicating the court ruled either simultaneously with or immediately after receiving opposition, which is an…",
      "body_md": "On August 12, Judge Bostwick entered an Order on Motion to Compel (Dkt. 366), resolving the compel motion Trustee Donald Lassman filed August 10 (Dkt. 359) — the same motion for which the court set a hearing on August 10 (Dkt. 360). The order arrived the same day an objection was filed at Dkt. 365, indicating the court ruled either simultaneously with or immediately after receiving opposition, which is an accelerated disposition consistent with a hearing having been held. The full text of Dkt. 366 is not in the pulled-document record, so the precise terms — granted, denied, or granted in part — cannot be stated with certainty from the materials available; that determination requires a direct PACER pull of Dkt. 366.\n\nWhat the docket sequence does establish is significant for recovery posture. The underlying compel motion (Dkt. 359) arose in the context of the pending appeal of the July 17 sale order (Dkt. 343), in which Samara CR Holdings and Kahan are challenging the bankruptcy court's approval of the PBTC Recovery Partners sale on due process, good-faith purchaser, and insider-conflict grounds (Dkt. 357). Discovery in that contested posture — particularly any Rule 2004 or adversary-style compelled production — bears directly on the evidentiary record appellants are assembling. If Dkt. 366 granted the compel motion, it could open or expand the document record available to appellants before the district court. If it denied or limited compelled production, it narrows that record and cuts against the appellants' ability to supplement the designation of record filed August 3 (Dkt. 357). Until Dkt. 366's operative language is confirmed, the recovery implication remains directionally meaningful but factually indeterminate.\n\nThe next concrete milestone is confirmation of whether a further hearing or compliance deadline runs from Dkt. 366; that date and any production deadline should be verified directly on the docket, as the order's terms will govern the pace of pre-appellate discovery.\n\n## Sources\n\n*No press sources were used. All propositions derive from the docket record and pulled document text, which are primary sources requiring no citation.*\n\n---\n\n*This briefing is provided for informational purposes by Turnpage Digital Markets and does not constitute legal advice.*",
